      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Inscr." corresp="#wit-d">Norðhymbra preosta lagu.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">The law of the Northumbrian priests</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-d">Northumbrian Priests' Law</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Satzung der Northumbrer-Priester.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Statute of the Northumbrian priests.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann's text is from D (Cambridge, Corpus Christi College 201, p. 43, after ‘Polity’ 25, in the same hand, c. 1060), the same manuscript as the modern edition. The heading is in red. Liebermann dates the text 1028–c. 1060 and places it at York. Clause number standardised from ‘Northu. Inscr.’.</note>
      </div>
